<title>FRANCE: Traders expect Jordan to buy more wheat.</title>
<headline>Traders expect Jordan to buy more wheat.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>European grain traders said they expected Jordan to come to the market in August and buy some 100,000 tonnes of American hard red winter wheat.</p>
<p>Amman has not called a tender but traders say there is talk of one towards August 12.</p>
<p>&quot;There is nothing official for the moment, but we are expecting them,&quot; a trader said.</p>
<p>On July 23, Jordan bought 100,000 U.S. wheat at $171.00 and $172.65 per tonne cost and freight for delivery in August and September.</p>
</text>
